WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.002
This query creates January, February, and March admission counts plus a total.

00:00:06.002 --> 00:00:09.642
The left join preserves patients with no admissions.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:14.417
Run the query and compare total admissions with the displayed month columns.

00:00:14.417 --> 00:00:19.902
If the dataset contains only those months, the totals should align with their sum.

00:00:19.902 --> 00:00:26.027
Connect this idea to a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:26.027 --> 00:00:31.522
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.522 --> 00:00:39.222
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:39.222 --> 00:00:44.882
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:44.882 --> 00:00:50.703
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
